[19:42:29] [INFO] This step investigates whether the host-mass dependence predicted by TEP can be recovered when the global M_B constraint in Pantheon+ is released. Three analyses are performed: a data-driven M_B fit per host mass bin, quantification of the SALT2 mass step correction absorption, and a forward model applying the TEP-predicted per-host M_B correction. The key discriminating observable is the residual mass step in m_b_corr after the SALT2 correction, compared to the TEP-predicted Delta_M_B from the Cepheid calibration bias difference between massive and low-mass hosts.
