[19:42:29] [PROCESS] Analysis 1 fits M_B separately for massive (log10 M*/Msun >= 10.0) and low-mass hosts by minimizing Hubble residual scatter against the LCDM prediction at two reference H0 values (73.0 and 67.4 km/s/Mpc). The residual mass step (massive minus low-mass) reveals how much host-mass dependence survives the SALT2 mass step correction already applied to m_b_corr.
